# Markdown Cross-Reference Standards

## Description

Enforce proper cross-document linking standards in markdown files. All references to other documents or sections MUST use explicit markdown link syntax with relative paths. Bare document names or vague references are prohibited.

**Scope**: All cross-document references, section links, and related documentation citations.

## Rule

Execute the following cross-reference requirements:

1. **Use explicit link syntax**: `[text](./path/to/file.md)` for all document references
2. **Prohibit bare document names**: Never reference documents by name alone ("See CONTRIBUTING.md")
3. **Prohibit bare URLs**: All URLs must have link text
4. **Use relative paths**:
   - Same directory: `./file.md`
   - Parent directory: `../file.md`
   - Grandparent: `../../file.md`
5. **Include file extensions**: Always use `.md` in links
6. **Use anchor syntax** for section references: `[text](./file.md#section-title)`
7. **Format anchors correctly**: Lowercase with dashes (`#my-section-title`)
8. **Validate link targets**: All referenced files and sections MUST exist

## Implementation

Cursor IDE will enforce this rule by:

- Validating link syntax in real-time during editing
- Detecting broken links and missing anchor targets
- Providing auto-completion for file paths relative to current document
- Suggesting anchor links based on existing headers in target files
- Highlighting bare document name references as violations
- Offering quick-fix actions to convert bare names to proper links

## Benefits

1. **Navigation Reliability**: Links work correctly in all markdown viewers (GitHub, GitLab, VS Code, web)
2. **Refactoring Safety**: IDEs can automatically update links when files move or rename
3. **Validation**: Broken links detected automatically via linting and CI/CD
4. **Clarity**: Explicit links show relationship structure between documents
5. **Discoverability**: Clear cross-references improve documentation navigation

## Examples

### ✅ Correct Cross-References

```markdown
See the [Setup section](./CONTRIBUTING.md#setup) for installation instructions.

For more details, refer to the [API documentation](./docs/api-reference.md).

Check the [configuration guide](../config/settings.md#database-configuration).

Review [authentication patterns](../../security/auth.md#oauth2-flow) for implementation.
```

### ❌ Incorrect Cross-References

```markdown
❌ See the "Setup" section in the contribution guide.
   (No explicit link)

❌ Refer to CONTRIBUTING.md for more details.
   (Document name without link syntax)

❌ See [this document](CONTRIBUTING.md).
   (Missing ./ for relative path)

❌ Check the setup documentation.
   (Vague reference, no link)

❌ Visit https://example.com/docs
   (Bare URL without link text)
```

### Anchor Link Examples

```markdown
✅ CORRECT:
# My Section Title

[Link to section](#my-section-title)
[Link in other file](./other.md#my-section-title)

❌ INCORRECT:
[Link with spaces](#My Section Title)  ❌ Spaces not converted to dashes
[Link with caps](#My-Section-Title)    ❌ Capitals not converted to lowercase
```

### Quick Fix Patterns

**Before (Violation)**:
```markdown
See the API Reference for authentication details.
Refer to SECURITY.md for security policies.
```

**After (Corrected)**:
```markdown
See the [API Reference](./docs/api-reference.md#authentication) for authentication details.
Refer to [SECURITY.md](./SECURITY.md) for security policies.
```
